From 5ee7484dafa27bf047d6a0208ada7f84234ef708 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:40:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep a story's homecoming lines out of the partner's death
 scene

The death of the partner, or a lost life, loads Jijimon's house (218, or 205 once the city has grown) behind the death
and rebirth scenes, and that load runs the screen's enter code. A story line added there for the next homecoming
(SkullGreymon or Angemon back in the city, what the city remembers) then played over the dying partner, with its
recruit message, before the egg choice.

The death's MAPHEAD section (1246) sets trigger 41 and the load of the death map consumes it in checkShopMap (the shop
library must not be loaded over the death overlays). Now that load also writes 1 into pstat 124 (PSTAT_DEATH_MAP_ENTRY),
and every other map load writes 0. The pstat is not saved and no script of the game reads it; the story compiler tests
it before a story's enter code on the two death screens.
---
 include/dw/pstat.h       | 4 ++++
 src/main/script_common.c | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/dw/pstat.h b/include/dw/pstat.h
index 3c4faba..8c9edb5 100644
--- a/include/dw/pstat.h
+++ b/include/dw/pstat.h
@@ -268,5 +268,9 @@
    out with both sides standing the battle ends and PSTAT_BATTLE_TIMED_OUT reads 1 (both are not saved) */
 #define PSTAT_BATTLE_TIMED_OUT		PSTAT_241
 #define PSTAT_BATTLE_TIME_LIMIT		PSTAT_242
+/* MOD (death map entry): 1 while the screen was loaded by the partner's death or lost life (Jijimon's house, 218 or 205,
+   where the death and rebirth scenes play), 0 after any other load; checkShopMap writes it on every map load (not saved).
+   A story's enter code on those screens tests it, so that it waits for a real homecoming */
+#define PSTAT_DEATH_MAP_ENTRY		PSTAT_124
 
 #endif
diff --git a/src/main/script_common.c b/src/main/script_common.c
index b026711..b26db56 100644
--- a/src/main/script_common.c
+++ b/src/main/script_common.c
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <dw/map.h>
 #include <dw/math.h>
 #include <dw/params.h>
+#include <dw/pstat.h>
 #include <dw/script.h>
 #include <dw/sound.h>
 #include <dw/species.h>
@@ -3144,10 +3145,14 @@ void checkShopMap(mapId)
 	uint8_t local;
 	int32_t i;
 
+	/* MOD (death map entry): trigger 41 is set by the death's MAPHEAD section (1246) and consumed by the load of the
+	   death map: the screen's enter code can tell that load from a homecoming (PSTAT_DEATH_MAP_ENTRY, pstat.h) */
 	if (isTriggerSet(0x29) == 1) {
 		unsetTrigger(0x29);
+		writePStat(PSTAT_DEATH_MAP_ENTRY, 1);
 		return;
 	}
+	writePStat(PSTAT_DEATH_MAP_ENTRY, 0);
 	for (i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
 		if (mapId == SHOP_MAPS[i]) {
 			loadDynamicLibrary(SHOP_REL, &local, 0, 0, 0);
-- 
2.55.0

